WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.194 --> 00:00:18.276
When the weather turned warm, the earl and his wife left Earlshall Park.

2
00:00:19.297 --> 00:00:21.818
They wanted to spend time in London with some family members.

3
00:00:23.099 --> 00:00:26.020
Most of the horses were left behind, including Ginger and me.

4
00:00:27.021 --> 00:00:32.124
Mr. York went with the earl, leaving a senior groom named Reuben Smith in charge of the stable.

5
00:00:33.536 --> 00:00:39.481
The earl's two oldest daughters, Lady Harriet and Lady Anne, stayed at home with one of their brothers

6
00:00:39.642 --> 00:00:41.944
and some cousins who had come to visit for the summer.

7
00:00:43.105 --> 00:00:47.548
Lady Harriet was a sickly young woman who never went out in the carriage and rarely showed her

8
00:00:47.589 --> 00:00:48.389
face outdoors.

9
00:00:49.730 --> 00:00:53.694
Her sister, Lady Anne, on the other hand, was as lively and healthy as could be.

10
00:00:54.935 --> 00:00:59.679
She loved to spend time outside, and she went riding as often as she could with her brothers

11
00:00:59.719 --> 00:01:00.160
and cousins.

12
00:01:02.096 --> 00:01:05.778
Soon she became my primary rider, renaming me Black Auster.

13
00:01:07.018 --> 00:01:08.599
I enjoyed our rides very much.

14
00:01:09.800 --> 00:01:11.681
Lady Anne was an excellent horsewoman.

15
00:01:12.781 --> 00:01:15.823
Her hands were light, and her mood was always cheerful.

16
00:01:16.963 --> 00:01:19.925
Her favorite riding companion was a cousin named Blantyre.

17
00:01:21.525 --> 00:01:26.388
While some of the young men liked to ride Ginger, Blantyre's favorite was a different mare known as

18
00:01:26.448 --> 00:01:32.201
Lizzie. Lizzie was a bright bay with a smooth, fast canter and a lively spirit.

19
00:01:34.022 --> 00:01:38.523
Young Blantyre was always telling anyone who would listen what a fine horse she was.

20
00:01:41.043 --> 00:01:46.185
But Ginger, who knew Lizzie better than I did, once told me that Lizzie was rather nervous.

21
00:01:47.965 --> 00:01:52.807
One day when Lady Anne came to the stable, she asked the groom to put the sidesaddle on

22
00:01:52.847 --> 00:01:57.668
Lizzie. The sidesaddle was the type of saddle always used by young women.

23
00:01:58.856 --> 00:02:01.878
Lady Anne also said that Blantyre could ride me that day.

24
00:02:03.899 --> 00:02:08.121
When the young man himself arrived, he seemed surprised and a bit uneasy.

25
00:02:08.141 --> 00:02:10.263
"What's going on?"

26
00:02:10.603 --> 00:02:11.603
he asked Lady Anne.

27
00:02:11.623 --> 00:02:13.765
"Are you tired of Black Auster?"

28
00:02:13.785 --> 00:02:16.086
"Of course not!"

29
00:02:16.546 --> 00:02:17.747
she replied with a laugh.

30
00:02:17.767 --> 00:02:21.169
"But I'm nice enough to let you ride him just this once.

31
00:02:22.389 --> 00:02:26.852
And after all the good things you've said about Lizzie, I can't wait to try her myself!"

32
00:02:28.092 --> 00:02:31.094
"I'm not sure that's a good idea," Blantyre said.

33
00:02:31.114 --> 00:02:35.857
"Lizzie is a charming creature, but she's much too nervous for a lady.

34
00:02:37.058 --> 00:02:38.859
I don't think it's safe for you to ride her.

35
00:02:39.440 --> 00:02:41.881
Please, let's have the saddles switched back."

36
00:02:43.222 --> 00:02:44.443
Lady Anne just laughed.

37
00:02:44.463 --> 00:02:50.187
"My dear cousin, you don't have to worry about my safety!"

38
00:02:50.567 --> 00:02:51.248
she exclaimed.

39
00:02:51.268 --> 00:02:54.490
"I've been riding since I was a baby.

40
00:02:54.510 --> 00:02:57.692
Now stop looking so worried and help me mount."

41
00:02:58.764 --> 00:03:00.745
Blantyre bit his lip, but said no more.

42
00:03:02.146 --> 00:03:05.668
He helped her into the saddle, handed her the reins, and then mounted me.

43
00:03:09.030 --> 00:03:11.731
We were riding toward the gate when we heard someone calling.

44
00:03:13.752 --> 00:03:15.033
It was one of the house servants.

45
00:03:15.053 --> 00:03:18.194
"Lady Harriet has a question for Dr.

46
00:03:18.395 --> 00:03:20.756
Ashley," he said, holding up a slip of paper.

47
00:03:20.776 --> 00:03:26.599
"Would you mind delivering this note to his house and bringing back an answer?"

48
00:03:26.619 --> 00:03:30.245
"Certainly," Blantyre said, taking the note.

49
00:03:30.705 --> 00:03:31.806
"We'd be happy to help."

50
00:03:33.167 --> 00:03:35.488
The village where the doctor lived was about a mile away.

51
00:03:37.289 --> 00:03:38.850
We rode along at a pleasant walk.

52
00:03:39.991 --> 00:03:44.173
Blantyre was a good rider, and I was enjoying the exercise in the fresh air.

53
00:03:45.374 --> 00:03:47.215
Lizzie seemed to be having a good time as well.

54
00:03:48.316 --> 00:03:50.217
She was giving Lady Anne no trouble at all.

55
00:03:53.139 --> 00:03:55.000
We pulled up in front of the doctor's gate.

56
00:03:55.968 --> 00:04:00.109
There was a short path leading between some tall evergreens that hid the house from view.

57
00:04:00.129 --> 00:04:04.290
"Go ahead and take the note in," Lady Anne told her cousin.

58
00:04:04.311 --> 00:04:06.511
"Lizzie and I will wait for you here.

59
00:04:07.651 --> 00:04:11.913
You can hang Black Auster's rein on the gate— he won't go anywhere without you."

60
00:04:13.133 --> 00:04:14.413
Blantyre looked dubious.

61
00:04:14.433 --> 00:04:16.654
"Are you sure you'll be all right?"

62
00:04:16.674 --> 00:04:18.555
"Of course.

63
00:04:18.675 --> 00:04:19.615
Now go!"

64
00:04:19.635 --> 00:04:21.796
she said with a laugh.

65
00:04:24.440 --> 00:04:26.841
Blantyre dismounted and hung my reins on the fence.

66
00:04:27.521 --> 00:04:29.042
Then he disappeared between the trees.

67
00:04:30.243 --> 00:04:33.344
Lizzie was standing quietly by the side of the road on a loose rein.

68
00:04:34.924 --> 00:04:37.225
Lady Anne was smiling and humming a cheerful tune.

69
00:04:38.386 --> 00:04:41.507
We were right across the road from an open gate leading into a field.

70
00:04:42.568 --> 00:04:48.410
While we were waiting for Blantyre to return, some horses suddenly came trotting across the field, jumping and

71
00:04:48.450 --> 00:04:52.352
kicking. A boy was chasing them, cracking a large whip.

72
00:04:54.528 --> 00:04:59.091
Before I knew what was happening, one of the horses spotted the open gate and darted through it.

73
00:05:00.012 --> 00:05:04.115
The boy saw the escape and raced over, yelling and cracking the whip loudly.

74
00:05:05.936 --> 00:05:09.219
The colt raced across the road, bumping into Lizzie's hind end.

75
00:05:09.699 --> 00:05:11.921
Just then the whip let out another loud crack.

76
00:05:12.801 --> 00:05:17.605
"Oh!" Lady Anne cried, barely hanging on to the saddle as her horse gave a violent kick.

77
00:05:18.766 --> 00:05:21.928
A second later Lizzie bolted down the road at a headlong gallop.
